---
import ReferenceLayout from "../layouts/ReferenceLayout.astro";
---

<ReferenceLayout
	title="Components"
	description="Accessible, framework-independent controls and states for Kinra web surfaces."
	current="Components"
>
	<header class="catalog-header">
		<div class="catalog-header__inner kin-frame">
			<h1 class="kin-title">Components</h1>
			<p class="catalog-header__summary">
				Controls, labels, notices, fields, tables, and states with stable
				semantic and focus contracts. Wayfinding, feedback, evidence, and layers
				have their own pages.
			</p>
		</div>
	</header>

	<div class="catalog-section kin-frame component-grid">
		<section
			class="component-group component-group--wide"
			aria-labelledby="buttons-heading"
		>
			<h2 id="buttons-heading">Buttons</h2>
			<p>
				One primary action per region. Quiet, ghost, and neutral buttons carry
				the rest; danger is reserved for destruction that cannot be undone.
			</p>
			<div class="kin-stack">
				<div class="kin-cluster" data-space="compact">
					<button class="kin-button kin-button--primary" type="button">
						Save changes
					</button>
					<button class="kin-button" type="button">Neutral</button>
					<button class="kin-button kin-button--quiet" type="button">
						Quiet
					</button>
					<button class="kin-button kin-button--ghost" type="button">
						Ghost
					</button>
					<button class="kin-button kin-button--danger" type="button">
						Delete repository
					</button>
					<button class="kin-button kin-button--primary" type="button" disabled>
						Disabled
					</button>
				</div>
				<div class="kin-cluster" data-space="compact">
					<button
						class="kin-button kin-button--primary"
						data-size="large"
						type="button"
					>
						Large
					</button>
					<button class="kin-button" type="button">Default</button>
					<button class="kin-button" data-size="compact" type="button">
						Compact
					</button>
					<button
						class="kin-button kin-button--icon"
						type="button"
						aria-label="Search"
					>
						<svg
							viewBox="0 0 24 24"
							aria-hidden="true"
							fill="none"
							stroke="currentColor"
							stroke-width="2"
						>
							<circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle>
							<path d="M20 20l-3.5-3.5"></path>
						</svg>
					</button>
					<button
						class="kin-button kin-button--icon"
						data-size="compact"
						type="button"
						aria-label="More options"
					>
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor">
							<circle cx="5" cy="12" r="1.5"></circle>
							<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.5"></circle>
							<circle cx="19" cy="12" r="1.5"></circle>
						</svg>
					</button>
					<button class="kin-button" type="button" aria-pressed="true">
						Pressed
					</button>
				</div>
				<div class="kin-cluster" data-space="compact">
					<div class="kin-button-group" role="group" aria-label="View">
						<button
							class="kin-button"
							data-size="compact"
							type="button"
							aria-pressed="true"
						>
							List
						</button>
						<button
							class="kin-button"
							data-size="compact"
							type="button"
							aria-pressed="false"
						>
							Board
						</button>
						<button
							class="kin-button"
							data-size="compact"
							type="button"
							aria-pressed="false"
						>
							Timeline
						</button>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="component-group" aria-labelledby="labels-heading">
			<h2 id="labels-heading">Badges and chips</h2>
			<p>
				A badge labels taxonomy or bounded state and is not interactive. A chip
				is a control: it filters, selects, or can be removed.
			</p>
			<div class="kin-stack">
				<div class="kin-cluster" data-space="compact" aria-label="Badge tones">
					<span class="kin-badge">Draft</span>
					<span class="kin-badge" data-tone="primary">Active</span>
					<span class="kin-badge" data-tone="reason">Review</span>
					<span class="kin-badge" data-tone="success">Verified</span>
					<span class="kin-badge" data-tone="warning">Attention</span>
					<span class="kin-badge" data-tone="error">Blocked</span>
					<span class="kin-badge" data-variant="solid" data-tone="primary"
						>Solid</span
					>
					<span class="kin-badge" data-numeric>v0.3.0</span>
				</div>
				<div class="kin-cluster" data-space="tight" aria-label="Filter chips">
					<button class="kin-chip" type="button" aria-pressed="true">All</button
					>
					<button class="kin-chip" type="button" aria-pressed="false"
						>Open</button
					>
					<button class="kin-chip" type="button" aria-pressed="false"
						>Merged</button
					>
					<span class="kin-chip">
						author:blake
						<button
							class="kin-chip__remove"
							type="button"
							aria-label="Remove author filter"
						>
							<svg
								viewBox="0 0 12 12"
								aria-hidden="true"
								fill="none"
								stroke="currentColor"
								stroke-width="1.5"
							>
								<path d="M2 2l8 8M10 2l-8 8"></path>
							</svg>
						</button>
					</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="component-group" aria-labelledby="status-heading">
			<h2 id="status-heading">Status</h2>
			<p>
				A square marker and a word. Running is the only state that moves,
				because it is the only one doing something.
			</p>
			<div class="kin-cluster" data-space="compact" aria-label="Status states">
				<span class="kin-status">Idle</span>
				<span class="kin-status" data-state="reason">Reasoning</span>
				<span class="kin-status" data-state="running">Running</span>
				<span class="kin-status" data-state="success">Complete</span>
				<span class="kin-status" data-state="warning">Degraded</span>
				<span class="kin-status" data-state="error">Failed</span>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="component-group" aria-labelledby="notices-heading">
			<h2 id="notices-heading">Notices</h2>
			<div class="kin-stack" data-space="compact">
				<div class="kin-notice" data-tone="reason">
					<p class="kin-notice__title">Human review remains required</p>
					<p class="kin-notice__body">
						The reasoning channel can prepare evidence, but it cannot approve
						this release.
					</p>
					<div class="kin-notice__actions">
						<button class="kin-button" data-size="compact" type="button">
							Open review
						</button>
						<button
							class="kin-button kin-button--ghost"
							data-size="compact"
							type="button"
						>
							Dismiss
						</button>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="kin-notice" data-tone="warning" data-density="compact">
					<p class="kin-notice__title">Two repositories are behind</p>
					<p class="kin-notice__body">
						Version state is expressed in words; colour reinforces rather than
						replaces the message.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="component-group" aria-labelledby="fields-heading">
			<h2 id="fields-heading">Fields</h2>
			<form
				class="component-form kin-stack"
				aria-label="Example repository form"
			>
				<div class="kin-field">
					<label class="kin-field__label" for="repository-name">
						Repository name
						<span class="kin-field__required">Required</span>
					</label>
					<p class="kin-field__hint" id="repository-name-hint">
						Use a short, durable project name.
					</p>
					<input
						class="kin-input"
						id="repository-name"
						name="repository-name"
						placeholder="project-name"
						aria-describedby="repository-name-hint"
						required
					/>
				</div>
				<div class="kin-field">
					<label class="kin-field__label" for="repository-url">
						Clone URL
						<span class="kin-field__optional">Optional</span>
					</label>
					<div class="kin-input-group">
						<span class="kin-input-group__affix">https://</span>
						<input
							class="kin-input"
							id="repository-url"
							name="url"
							placeholder="depot.kinra.ai/blake/kin"
						/>
						<button class="kin-button" type="button">Copy</button>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="kin-field">
					<label class="kin-field__label" for="visibility">Visibility</label>
					<select class="kin-select" id="visibility" name="visibility">
						<option>Private</option>
						<option>Public</option>
					</select>
				</div>
				<div class="kin-field">
					<label class="kin-field__label" for="notes">Notes</label>
					<textarea
						class="kin-textarea"
						id="notes"
						name="notes"
						placeholder="What should a reviewer know?"></textarea>
				</div>
				<div class="kin-field">
					<label class="kin-field__label" for="branch">Branch</label>
					<input
						class="kin-input"
						id="branch"
						name="branch"
						value="main"
						aria-invalid="true"
						aria-describedby="branch-error"
					/>
					<p class="kin-field__error" id="branch-error">
						A branch named main already exists.
					</p>
				</div>
				<label class="kin-check">
					<input type="checkbox" name="readme" checked />
					<span>
						Create the repository with a README
						<span class="kin-check__hint">You can change this later.</span>
					</span>
				</label>
			</form>
		</section>

		<section class="component-group" aria-labelledby="choice-heading">
			<h2 id="choice-heading">Switch, range, and segmented</h2>
			<p>
				All three wrap native inputs. The switch is a checkbox with
				<code>role="switch"</code>; the segmented control is a radio group.
			</p>
			<div class="kin-stack">
				<label class="kin-switch">
					<input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked />
					<span>Allow the peer to open pull requests</span>
				</label>
				<label class="kin-switch">
					<input type="checkbox" role="switch" />
					<span>Publish release notes automatically</span>
				</label>
				<div class="kin-field">
					<label class="kin-field__label" for="context">Context window</label>
					<input
						class="kin-range"
						id="context"
						type="range"
						min="4"
						max="128"
						value="32"
					/>
					<p class="kin-field__hint">32k tokens</p>
				</div>
				<fieldset class="kin-fieldset">
					<legend class="kin-fieldset__legend">Density</legend>
					<div class="kin-segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Density">
						<label>
							<input type="radio" name="density" value="comfortable" checked />
							<span>Comfortable</span>
						</label>
						<label>
							<input type="radio" name="density" value="compact" />
							<span>Compact</span>
						</label>
						<label>
							<input type="radio" name="density" value="dense" />
							<span>Dense</span>
						</label>
					</div>
				</fieldset>
				<fieldset class="kin-fieldset" data-variant="bounded">
					<legend class="kin-fieldset__legend">Notify me when</legend>
					<label class="kin-check">
						<input type="checkbox" name="notify" checked />
						<span>A review is requested</span>
					</label>
					<label class="kin-check">
						<input type="checkbox" name="notify" />
						<span>A release is tagged</span>
					</label>
				</fieldset>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="component-group" aria-labelledby="disclosure-heading">
			<h2 id="disclosure-heading">Native disclosure</h2>
			<details class="kin-disclosure" open>
				<summary>What remains source-owned?</summary>
				<div class="kin-disclosure__body">
					<p>
						Routes, copy, product claims, workflows, analytics, and deployment
						remain with the repository that owns their outcome.
					</p>
				</div>
			</details>
			<details class="kin-disclosure">
				<summary>When does a component become stable?</summary>
				<div class="kin-disclosure__body">
					<p>
						After two real consumers demonstrate the same responsibility and the
						contract survives accessibility and responsive review.
					</p>
				</div>
			</details>
			<div style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
				<details class="kin-disclosure" data-variant="panel">
					<summary>Panel variant</summary>
					<div class="kin-disclosure__body">
						<p>A bounded box for settings groups and advanced options.</p>
					</div>
				</details>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section
			class="component-group component-group--wide"
			aria-labelledby="table-heading"
		>
			<div class="catalog-heading">
				<h2 id="table-heading">Inspectable data</h2>
				<p>
					Tables keep native semantics and horizontal containment. Numeric
					columns align right with tabular figures; a selected row carries the
					primary edge.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="kin-table-wrap">
				<table class="kin-table">
					<caption>Current package contracts</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">Layer</th>
							<th scope="col">Distribution</th>
							<th scope="col">State</th>
							<th scope="col" data-align="numeric">Classes</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td data-emphasis>Foundations</td>
							<td>Versioned CSS</td>
							<td><span class="kin-badge" data-tone="success">Stable</span></td>
							<td data-align="numeric">14</td>
						</tr>
						<tr aria-selected="true">
							<td data-emphasis>Components</td>
							<td>Versioned CSS</td>
							<td
								><span class="kin-badge" data-tone="primary">Expanded</span></td
							>
							<td data-align="numeric">41</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td data-emphasis>Patterns</td>
							<td>Copied source</td>
							<td
								><span class="kin-badge" data-tone="reason">Candidate</span></td
							>
							<td data-align="numeric">3</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
					<tfoot>
						<tr>
							<td colspan="3">Total</td>
							<td data-align="numeric">58</td>
						</tr>
					</tfoot>
				</table>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section
			class="component-group component-group--wide"
			aria-labelledby="empty-heading"
		>
			<h2 id="empty-heading">Empty state</h2>
			<div class="kin-empty">
				<p class="kin-empty__title">No release candidates</p>
				<p class="kin-empty__body">
					Explain what the empty collection means and offer an action only when
					there is a legitimate next step.
				</p>
				<button class="kin-button kin-button--quiet" type="button">
					Prepare a candidate
				</button>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</ReferenceLayout>
